    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>h(x,y,z) = xy\frac{1}{z^{2}}, \left(2,5,5\right), \left(-6,-2,4\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,5,5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-6,-2,4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.75</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y,z) = \left(2,5,5\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(2,5,5) = 2 \cdot 5 \cdot \frac{1}{5^{2}} = \frac{10}{25} = 0.4</m>.



For the second point, substitute <m>(x,y,z) = \left(-6,-2,4\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(-6,-2,4) = -6 \cdot -2 \cdot \frac{1}{4^{2}} = \frac{12}{16} = 0.75</m>.





</solution>
